To display the latitude and longitude of a given location on a map using PHP, we can use the Google Maps API. This is relevant to the study of geography because it allows us to visualize and understand the location of a place on a map.
Here is a sample code snippet that utilizes the Google Maps API to display the latitude and longitude of a given location:
```php
<?php
$address = "1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043"; // the address of the location we want to display
$apiKey = "YOUR_API_KEY"; // your Google Maps API key
// create the URL for the Google Maps API request
$url = "https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?address=" . urlencode($address) . "&key=" . $apiKey;
// make the API request and decode the JSON response
$response = json_decode(file_get_contents($url), true);
// extract the latitude and longitude from the response
$lat = $response['results'][0]['geometry']['location']['lat'];
$lng = $response['results'][0]['geometry']['location']['lng'];
// display the latitude and longitude on a map using the Google Maps API
echo "<iframe src='https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?q=" . urlencode($address) . "&zoom=15&key=" . $apiKey . "&center=" . $lat . "," . $lng . "' width='600' height='450' frameborder='0' style='border:0' allowfullscreen></iframe>";
?>
```
